  "notes": [
    "AFI_SOCIO.NUMERO_AFILIACION is the canonical unprefixed Fineract externalId and cross-service client mapping key; company/branch/ID_SOCIO remain the Arissto relational join.",
    "The clients service migrates natural-person identity, KYC/profile datatables, and identifiers; loans and deposit accounts are excluded.",
    "Home and work addresses remain plain text in the reviewed KYC datatables. The Fineract structured address module is intentionally out of scope.",
    "Duplicate phone numbers and duplicate DUI values are valid and are preserved. Duplicate passport, NIT, and residency identifiers remain quarantined.",
    "Malformed source emails are omitted from the Fineract core client instead of quarantining the client.",
    "Arissto economic-activity key 0 is a missing-value sentinel and is migrated as null; other unresolved nonzero activity keys remain quarantined.",
    "Catalog-backed text and target IDs are resolved from the target database crosswalk created by Liquibase migration 0272; target-generated IDs are never hard-coded.",
    "Sparse datatable rows are not created when every mapped value is null.",
    "Unverified semantics remain explicitly excluded rather than guessed: US citizenship, PEP relation details, housing type/tenure, remittance relationship/time units, periodicity labels, and calculated totals.",
    "All imported Arissto clients are active in Fineract. AFI_SOCIO.FECHA_REGISTRO is used as the historical activation date, except when it predates the target office opening date; those records use the office opening date, the earliest value Fineract permits.",
    "Every imported client receives exactly one tipo_cliente tag. AFI_SOCIO relationship 003 maps to cliente; relationship 001 maps to socio unless the party has an originated CRD_CARTERA credit, in which case it maps to cliente-socio.",
    "Penalties, balances, schedules, interest, loans, deposits, and other product/calculated values are excluded."
  ]
